&#8220;I was playing one the other day and this one actually has Hov on it,&#8221; Mary teased during her appearance on 7PM in Brooklyn Monday (Jan. 19). &#8220;And It&#8217;s a monster, too! When we were younger, we were amped recording that record. I&#8217;m not gonna say who it was, but somebody leaked it and then we couldn&#8217;t do anything with it.&#8221;

However, Mary left the door open to possibly revisiting the shelved collaboration all these years later. &#8220;Hov, he felt disrespected that someone from my session had leaked it,&#8221; she explained. &#8220;But maybe we could revisit it.&#8221;

While the Queen of Hip-Hop Soul and Jay missed connecting that time around, they did join forces for Reasonable Doubt &#8216;s &#8220;Cant Knock the Hustle,&#8221; as well as Mary&#8217;s The Breakthrough album in 2005 for &#8220;Can&#8217;t Hide From Luv&#8221; and 2003&#8217;s Love & Life intro.

Mary J. Blige and the Brooklyn rapper headed out on the co-headlining Heart of the City Tour in 2008 following the arrival of Mary&#8217;s Growing Pains album and Jay-Z&#8217;s American Gangster LP the year prior. The trek took over arenas across North American, including three dates at New York&#8217;s Madison Square Garden.

The Grammy-winning artist will be taking her talents to Sin City this summer, where she&#8217;ll be playing her first-ever Las Vegas residency. The &#8220;Real Love&#8221; singer&#8217;s Mary J. Blige: My Life, My Story The Las Vegas Residency will hit the Dolby Live at Park MGM stage for 10 shows, which kicks off on May 1 and runs through July.

